# GitHub Workflow Orchestration

Follow this after local agent phases complete (see `.cursor/rules/workflow-orchestration.mdc`). Use `gh` for all GitHub operations.

## Branch strategy

- `main` is protected — never force-push
- Features: `feat/<scope>-<short-name>` (e.g. `feat/crm-leads`)
- Fixes: `fix/<scope>-<short-name>`
- Infra/docs: `chore/<short-name>`

## PR phase gate

Do not open a PR until upstream artifacts exist:

- `docs/prd/<feature>.md` (or approved foundation docs for scaffold work)
- `docs/architecture/<feature>.md`
- `docs/design/<feature>.md` (for UI changes)

Phase 5 (`test-engineer`) must produce a test report before PR creation.

## PR requirements

Every PR body must include:

```markdown
## Summary
- <1-3 bullets describing why>

## Docs
- <paths to prd/architecture/design touched>

## Test plan
- [ ] <checklist mapped to P0 acceptance criteria>
```

Use `gh pr create` with a HEREDOC body. Link related issues when applicable.

## CI expectations

When `.github/workflows/` exists, required pipeline order:

1. **Lint** — ESLint, Prettier, typecheck
2. **Test** — unit + API integration
3. **Build** — all apps and packages compile

Block merge if any check fails or P0 tests are missing.  
`devops-engineer` owns workflow YAML; follow this rule for job order and PR gates.

## Agent mapping

| Agent phase | GitHub action |
|-------------|---------------|
| `test-engineer` | Test report pasted into PR test plan |
| `devops-engineer` | Docker/CI config in PR; future Actions YAML |
| User / agent | Push branch, open PR, monitor checks |

## gh CLI rules

- Use `gh` for PRs, checks, issues, releases
- Check CI: `gh pr checks <number>`
- Never `git push --force` to `main`
- Only create commits when the user explicitly requests

## Shipping handoff

End implementation work with:

```
## GitHub Handoff
- **Branch**: feat/...
- **PR**: <url or "ready to open">
- **CI**: pending | green | failed (with failing job)
- **Docs referenced**: docs/prd/..., docs/architecture/..., docs/design/...
```
